{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For am I in the place of Elohim, etc.</b> The meaning is: if you are liable to punishment for the matter, Elohim is the judge, and I will neither take revenge nor bear a grudge. And the reason he did not forgive them is possibly because among the descendants of Noah the matter does not depend on their forgiveness — when a person sins against another, as for example if he robbed him and the victim forgives him, the robber is not exempt from the death penalty. Or even in the case of Israel: if an Israelite stole a fellow Israelite and sold him, it is not in the power of the stolen person to exempt the kidnapper from death. And he further said to them that there is room to judge them favorably."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:51:23.578189918Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}